-- Fixture for the `l4 export --to=bpmn` rule-selection tests.
--
-- A BPMN document holds exactly one process, and `L4.Bpmn.Emit.renderBpmn`
-- writes its own `<?xml ...?>` prolog, so two of them concatenated is not a
-- well-formed document. This file therefore has TWO regulative rules:
--
--   * `l4 export --to=bpmn` with no --rule must refuse and name both rules;
--   * `--rule "the fee"` must pick one of them.

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Filer, Registrar

DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
  `file the return`
  `acknowledge the return`
  `pay the fee`

`the filing` MEANS
  PARTY Filer
  MUST `file the return`
  WITHIN 30
  HENCE PARTY Registrar MUST `acknowledge the return` WITHIN 7

`the fee` MEANS
  PARTY Filer
  MUST `pay the fee`
  WITHIN 14
